meta {
  name: Registry
}

headers {
  ~X-External-User-Id: {{devUserExternalId}}
}

auth {
  mode: oauth2
}

auth:oauth2 {
  grant_type: authorization_code
  callback_url: {{oauthCallbackUrl}}
  authorization_url: {{authBrowserUrl}}/oauth2/authorize
  access_token_url: {{authBrowserUrl}}/oauth2/token
  refresh_token_url: {{authBrowserUrl}}/oauth2/token
  client_id: {{oauthPkceClientId}}
  client_secret: 
  scope: {{oauthScopes}}
  state: 
  pkce: true
  credentials_placement: body
  credentials_id: credentials
  token_source: access_token
  token_placement: header
  token_header_prefix: Bearer
  auto_fetch_token: true
  auto_refresh_token: false
}

docs {
  # Registry API collection

  Covers Registry (GraphQL + REST), Registry Auth (OAuth2/OIDC, GraphQL, REST),
  Registry Rollup (GraphQL), privileged admin operations, and a Bootstrap folder
  used to seed/verify a fresh local or cloud stack.

  ## Auth model
  The collection root authenticates with **OAuth2 Authorization Code + PKCE**
  against Registry Auth using the seeded public client (`oauthPkceClientId`).
  Every folder/request uses `auth: inherit` unless it needs something else:

  * `Registry Auth / Registered Clients` and `Bootstrap` admin calls use the
    `X-Api-Secret` header (`apiSecret`) instead of a bearer token.
  * The commented `X-External-User-Id` header is the Registry **local/test
    profile dev-auth bypass**. Enable it (remove `~`) to skip OAuth entirely
    when Registry runs with the `local` profile.

  ## Environments
  * `Local` – everything on localhost (Registry 8100, Auth 8200, Rollup 8150).
  * `Cloud` – placeholder hostnames; fill in via `.env`.

  All secrets and site-specific values come from `.env` (gitignored).
  Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the values.
}
